nish-office/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kform-danish-office/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kform-danish-office/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kform-danish-office/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":92019116,"digest":"sha256:bf89e82a2d02c133c9bab7b6324575766e248f6b629a64d2fb822aafad5e0524","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:07:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T09:08:03Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/kform-danish-office/Thesis/releases/download/thesis-v1-v2-v3-review/Thesis_V1_V2_V3_Source.zip"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kform-danish-office/Thesis/tarball/thesis-v1-v2-v3-review","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kform-danish-office/Thesis/zipball/thesis-v1-v2-v3-review","body":"Revised full thesis covering the development from the V1/G071 prototype through the integrated V2/F410 board and the slimmer V3 edge-card design.\n\nDownloads:\n- **Thesis_V1_V2_V3.pdf** — complete 434-page thesis, including the V2 schematics and all 31 PCB print pages.\n- **Thesis_V1_V2_V3_Source.zip** — current editable XeLaTeX project, figures, measurement records and supporting source (486 files).\n- **SHA256SUMS.txt** — checksums for both downloads.\n\nThe V3 discussion includes the estimated 8% net volume reduction after removing the USB-PD section, the secondary-winding observations and suspected input-current-path bottleneck. Replacement magnetics and V3 continuous-power validation remain unfinished. The 240 W EPR level is a future development goal.\n\nThe source ZIP attached above contains the current thesis work. GitHub's automatic “Source code” archives represent the older repository checkout associated with the tag.\n\nValidation: full XeLaTeX/latexmk build; no undefined references or citations, missing characters, overfull boxes or physical-page text overflow. All four current V2 schematic sheets and 31 PCB pages verified in the PDF. Source ZIP CRCs and every member hash verified.\n\n\nReader introduction: electronics and MCU pins are explained before pin identifiers are used. The signal map distinguishes G071/F410 roles, and ADC, timers, DMA and serial communication are introduced in plain language.\n\n\nEditorial update: removed the paired no-load development oscilloscope photographs and their references. Routine prose now uses MCU; specific model names remain for comparisons, component identification and exact build details.\n"}